From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:35:27 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 23/30] WMF: DXVA decoding on feature level 9_3, frames read
 back to memory

Hardware decoding was off on the Lumia 650 because texture sharing needs
feature level 10_0, and every video was decoded in software. This port is
one process, so DXVA can decode on its own device with no sharing at all:
hardware decoding is no longer disabled for want of texture sharing, and
WMFVideoMFTManager then reads each NV12 frame back through IMF2DBuffer
and hands it on as a software frame (NV12 added to CreateBasicVideoFrame,
the chroma plane placed after the decoder surface's own height, no
video-processor configuration). The log says "frames read back to memory".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../platforms/wmf/WMFVideoMFTManager.cpp      | 61 ++++++++++++++-----
 dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFVideoMFTManager.h  |  4 ++
 gfx/thebes/gfxWindowsPlatform.cpp             |  7 +++
 3 files changed, 57 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFVideoMFTManager.cpp b/dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFVideoMFTManager.cpp
